[00:00.83]Lesson 34 | 第34课
[00:02.71]Adolescence | 青春期
[00:10.30]What do adolescents respect in parents? | 青少年尊重父母的什么品质？
[00:16.18]Parents are often upset when their children praise the homes of their friends and regard it as a slur on their own cooking, or cleaning, or furniture, | 当孩子称赞朋友的家时，父母常常感到不安，把它看作是对自家的饭菜、清洁或家具的诋毁，
[00:26.68]and often are foolish enough to let the adolescents see that they are annoyed. | 而且往往愚蠢得让青少年看出自己恼火。
[00:32.24]They may even accuse them of disloyalty, or make some spiteful remark about the friends' parents. | 他们甚至可能指责孩子不忠，或者对朋友的父母说些刻薄的话。
[00:39.58]Such a loss of dignity and descent into childish behaviour on the part of the adults deeply shocks the adolescents, | 成年人这种有失体面、堕入幼稚行为的表现深深地震动了青少年，
[00:48.13]and makes them resolve that in future they will not talk to their parents about the places or people they visit. | 使他们决心今后不再同父母谈论自己访问的地方或见到的人。
[00:55.96]Before very long the parents will be complaining that the child is so secretive and never tells them anything, | 要不了多久，父母就会抱怨孩子遮遮掩掩，从不告诉他们任何事情，
[01:03.19]but they seldom realize that they have brought this on themselves. | 但他们很少意识到这是他们自己造成的。
[01:08.63]Disillusionment with the parents, | 对父母的幻想破灭，
[01:11.02]however good and adequate they may be both as parents and as individuals, is to some degree inevitable. | 无论父母作为父母和作为个人多么称职，在一定程度上是不可避免的。
[01:20.05]Most children have such a high ideal of their parents, | 大多数孩子对父母抱有如此之高的理想，
[01:23.92]unless the parents themselves have been unsatisfactory, that it can hardly hope to stand up to a realistic evaluation. | 除非父母本身就不称职，否则这种理想几乎无法经受住现实的检验。
[01:31.85]Parents would be greatly surprised and deeply touched if they realized how much belief their children usually have in their character and infallibility, | 倘若父母意识到孩子通常多么相信他们的品格和一贯正确，以及这种信赖对孩子意味着什么，
[01:42.99]and how much this faith means to a child. | 他们会大为吃惊并深受感动。
[01:46.55]If parents were prepared for this adolescent reaction, | 倘若父母对这种青春期的反应有思想准备，
[01:50.44]and realized that was a sign that the child was growing up | 并意识到这标志着孩子正在长大，
[01:54.22]and developing valuable powers of observation and independent judgment, | 正在发展宝贵的观察力和独立判断的能力，
[01:59.73]they would not be so hurt, and therefore would not drive the child into opposition by resenting and resisting it. | 他们就不会那么伤心，也就不会因怨恨和抵制这种反应而把孩子推向对立面。
[02:08.75]The adolescent, with his passion for sincerity, | 青少年热诚地崇尚真诚，
[02:12.93]always respects a parent who admits that he is wrong, or ignorant, | 总是尊重承认自己错了、或者无知、
[02:17.85]or even that he has been unfair or unjust. | 甚至承认自己一直不公平或不公正的父母。
[02:21.39]What the child cannot forgive is the parents' refusal to admit these charges if the child knows them to be true. | 孩子所不能原谅的，是父母拒绝承认这些指责，如果孩子知道这些指责属实的话。
[02:31.04]Victorian parents believed that they kept their dignity by retreating behind an unreasoning authoritarian attitude in fact they did nothing of the kind, | 维多利亚时代的父母相信，退回到蛮不讲理的专制作风背后就能保住尊严，其实他们根本没有做到这一点，
[02:41.84]but children were then too cowed to let them know how they really felt. | 只不过当时的孩子被吓住了，不敢让他们知道自己真正的感受。
[02:46.92]Today we tend to go to the other extreme, | 今天我们往往走向另一个极端，
[02:50.30]but on the whole this is a healthier attitude both for the child and the parent. | 但总的来说，无论对孩子还是对父母，这是一种更为健康的态度。
[02:56.57]It is always wiser and safer to face up to reality, however painful it may be at the moment. | 不管眼下多么痛苦，正视现实总是更明智、更安全的。
